Experiment No.: 01

Experiment Name: Introduction to Git and GitHub: Repository Creation, FileManagement, Commit and Integration with Visual Studio Code

1. Course Topics

In this course, we will learn the following web programming languages and technologies:

- HTML (HyperText Markup Language):** Used to create the structure of web pages.
- CSS (Cascading Style Sheets):** Used to design and style web pages.
- JavaScript:** Used to make web pages interactive and dynamic.
- PHP (Hypertext Preprocessor):** Used for server-side programming and data processing.

2. GitHub Account and Lab Submission

GitHub will be used as the main platform for maintaining our lab activities. Our teacher gave us the following instructions:

- Each student must create a personal GitHub account.
- Completed lab tasks must be uploaded to GitHub regularly.
- All lab work should be properly organized in repositories.
- GitHub will be used for submitting regular lab assignments.

3. Course Project

At the end of the semester, every student must prepare and submit a final project using the knowledge gained from the lab classes. The project is expected to cover the technologies learned throughout the course.
